00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:05.110 align:start position:0%
 
monsters walk among us  i might still be a monster  but i'm an evolving monster  hey guys pete here there's an official  trailer out for dexter new blood and i'm  going to give that a closer look as  there's a lot of interesting stuff going  on it gives us our first real glimpses  of both harrison and deb and overall  it's the most complete and exciting  thing they put out so far i'm gonna  break it down and i'm gonna tie that in  with all the other things we've heard  about the dexter revival so if any of  that sounds like spoilers to you then  this is your chance to leave  the full trailer builds on the teasers  that came before it revisiting and  extending some of the shots which adds  more context there's also a lot of brand  new stuff which gives us a better idea  about the story of the new season it  opens with dexter getting pulled over  while driving his truck into town  there's a knife on his passenger seat  and he looks nervous but no need to  worry it's really just his girlfriend  playing around she's the chief of police  in this fictional small town where he  lives iron lake new york which has a  population of less than 3 000 residents  you get the impression that dex who's  now living under the assumed name jim  lindsey is managing to fit in he works  at the local fish and game store he's  still the donut guy or maybe it's the  cinnamon roll guy now and he seems to be  well known and well liked around town in  the voiceover he says this is my life a  wolf among sheep from what michael c  hall and showrunner clyde phillips have  said in interviews dexter is trying to  keep his urges to kill under control and  part of that is relocating himself to  this remote place with less people and  therefore less potential victims they've  also hinted that something will happen  to cause him to fear that his dark  passenger will reveal itself in one of  the previous teasers you could see a  reflection of a victim wrapped in  plastic on a kill table as he stood in  front of a window and here you could see  he's throwing hefty bags into a fire in  an effort to destroy evidence and we  will come back to that one of the new  sequences we see is his girlfriend  angela hanging up a missing person sign  in the police station when dexter asks  her about it we get the impression that  this is a case that's ongoing and she  has no bodies no pattern someone's  getting away with making people  disappear there's a shot of a girl  hitchhiking at night she gets picked up  by a semi and you hear angela say people  don't just disappear there's always a  reason which is funny considering dexter  faked his own death so he could  disappear there's a lot of shots of him  running around looking at knives  sharpening his blades that sort of stuff  they're all mixed in there in the  background as he thinks about the  potential of someone being out there  that he could justifiably kill he's  thinking about what angela said he says  if she's right how many other victims  are there  there's a lot here that invokes the  humor of the series his awkwardness  around other people and then there's  this shot where he crosses off the date  on his calendar with a red marker and it  spills out dripping on the floor like  blood there's quite a few calendars  there there's at least six of them  hanging on his wall where you can see  that he was crossing off the dates i'm  not sure if that's to indicate how many  days he's been in iron lake or how long  it's been since he had his last kill and  you get the idea when he's looking at  the marker dripping on the floor that  he's reaching his breaking point in the  first dialogue we hear from deb it  sounds like she's addressing that same  struggle she says you're a serial killer  you love that you're getting away with  murder and you cannot wait to kill again  have you learned nothing all of this  appears to be connected to that kill and  the disposal of the body now that he  can't throw them in the ocean anymore it  looks like he burns the remains of his  victims but based on what deb's saying  i'm wondering if this is a one-off maybe  related to that shot of the police  busting into this house you see there's  a person slumped over in a chair here  who looks like he was a drug dealer i  could see this shot of dexter hitting  someone in the last teaser being  connected to that maybe this guy had  something to do with the drug dealer and  maybe that's where dex feels justified  in taking this guy out not exactly sure  how that would jive with him not acting  on his urges but we'll have to wait and  see it's a little curious because they  said they wanted to switch things up to  get out of that big bat of the season  kind of framework that they had been  stuck in but this all sort of looks like  a serial killer in town with the  addition of a kill of the week so maybe  what they're saying is that there'll be  hints of that but it won't be the crux  of the entire season  there's also some more shots at this  crime scene in the woods angela is  behind the crime scene tape looking at a  pool of blood on the snow and one of the  other cops makes a joke about dexter  being queasy at the sight of blood  there's also the first shot we've seen  of jamie chung she's taking a selfie at  the crime scene we know her character is  being described as a famous true crime  podcaster which would probably have a  pretty big social media presence all of  that makes you wonder if someone from  his old life will recognize dexter's  photo online  we also see this shot of a woman coming  out of an underground cellar to me it  looks like the same woman from the  missing poster and you see this ski mask  killer who has a rifle with the laser  scope he's popped up in the other  teasers i saw some comments saying this  character is probably based on the  serial killer robert hansen who killed  at least 17 women in anchorage alaska in  the 70s and early 80s his mo was to pick  up sex workers and take them to his  remote cabin at gunpoint where he would  rape them and then release them in a  secluded area to hunt them like wild  game before shooting or stabbing them it  looks like this might be what the  mystery man's doing as well as we see  the girl run through the snow before  getting shot it makes you wonder about  the shots we've seen of dexter in the  woods with the hunting rifle and there's  another shot of him in this trailer  where he's running in a wooded area  there's a couple of weird shots i can't  make much out of there's a person who  comes up to one of dexter's windows in  his cabin and knocks on it with a bullet  and then there's this other shot of a  kid looking through something like a  mail slot in a door as the mystery man  pulls on a ski mask we hear dexter say  monsters walk among us i might still be  a monster but i'm an evolving monster  and i can't wait to find out what he's  thinking about there  one of the most exciting scenes is deb  looking at evidence on the floor of  dexter's cabin this sort of makes it  look like she's a real person or alive  or something along those lines but the  creators have confirmed that she is in  his head similar to how harry used to be  in that capacity she seems to be looking  at evidence trying to solve the case  there's pictures of blood on the snow  similar to what we saw angela looking at  earlier you can also see these pieces of  red string at the crime scenes it looks  like that's the killer's calling card  and next to those photos there's five  photos of people you see dexter and  angela and then three new characters  clancy brown who's playing kirk caldwell  the owner of a local truck stop who is a  sort of unofficial mayor of the small  town what looks like this guy who shows  up a little later in the trailer with a  rifle and some blood on his face and  this other guy who we saw waving a knife  around kind of joking about it at  dexter's job  in a final scene that follows the title  and the release date dexter comes into  his cabin and finds a teenager inside  looking at his stuff when he asks him  what he's doing he finds out it's his  son harrison  they did give this away a couple weeks  ago they confirmed that it was harrison  and that he would show up in the first  episode and what's crazy about seeing it  is how that's going to work with  everything else that we've already seen  in my last video i talked about how  clyde phillips told the tca that there  wasn't a way to go back and revisit  dexter without including the theme of  fathers and sons and so here we get a  look at their reintroduction now it  would probably take a whole another  video to get into all the different  speculation about how this might work  how harrison figured out he wasn't dead  how he was able to track him down in  upstate new york how old is he really  because he should only be about 13 years  old and they're obviously aging him up  some here but as far as this video is  concerned you could see that his  presence is going to make things even  more complicated in dexter's life and  that's all the big stuff we see in the  trailer when i was looking at what  people were talking about after it  dropped i noticed some people wondering  if deb was really alive or if maybe the  kid in his apartment is someone else  pretending to be harrison unless  everyone involved with the show is  willfully misdirecting us then i don't  expect either one of those things to be  the case they've said in multiple  interviews that deb is essentially  taking harry's place and that dexter and  harrison coming back together as a main  focal point of the season they also said  they weren't changing anything that  already happened and deb definitely did  die in the finale it all looks great  this trailer especially looked pretty  impressive and it contrasts so well with  the old setting in miami and the old  dexter each new thing they put out  increases my interest in revisiting this  character i think i probably will put  together a harrison video because it's a  little hard to say right now how well  that's gonna go over out of everything  that we've seen it's the one thing that  feels like it might not work at this  point but i suppose the idea that they  have they thought it was essential and  they thought it was a good enough reason  to bring the series back the rest of the  new characters all look pretty  interesting  i like the idea of bringing someone in  who has a platform obviously this  podcaster might be looking into the  trinity killer and considering that rita  was one of his victims that might make  an exciting situation i mean she  wouldn't be in upstate new york for that  it looks like she's probably coming for  this new killer but you can see how any  attention from her or her followers  would be potentially awful for dexter  and i think that's a good place to leave  things let me know in the comments what  you thought about the new trailer what  you're hoping to see what are your  theories please like this video if you  enjoyed it please subscribe to my  channel if you haven't already thanks  for watching i'll talk to you soon

